  "fbaf67cf-bde1-4ef3-a69d-265caeb5f302": {
   "id": "fbaf67cf-bde1-4ef3-a69d-265caeb5f302",
   "message": {
    "id": "fbaf67cf-bde1-4ef3-a69d-265caeb5f302",
    "author": {
     "role": "assistant",
     "name": null,
     "metadata": {}
    },
    "create_time": 1762980771.406,
    "update_time": null,
    "content": {
     "content_type": "text",
     "parts": [
      "Two separate problems here:\n\n**1. Why it disconnects (code 1006, ~40 s):** 1006 is an abnormal close with no close frame, which usually means something in the middle killed an idle connection. ~40 s of silence lines up with a proxy/load-balancer idle timeout. If section B is on a different network segment or goes through a different proxy (e.g., the lab's wifi vs wired, or a campus proxy), that explains A vs B.\n\nQuick fix: send an application-level heartbeat more often than the timeout.\n\n```js\n// client\nlet hb;\nsocket.addEventListener(\"open\", () => {\n  hb = setInterval(() => socket.readyState === 1 && socket.send(JSON.stringify({ t: \"ping\" })), 20000);\n});\nsocket.addEventListener(\"close\", () => clearInterval(hb));\n```\n\nIf you use socket.io, set `pingInterval: 15000, pingTimeout: 10000` on the server instead.\n\n**2. Why you lose events (the bigger bug):** your log says `flush: 0 queued events` after reconnect, so events emitted while the socket was closed aren't being queued. Probably your `send()` does `if (socket.readyState === OPEN) socket.send(...)` and silently drops otherwise.\n\n```js\nconst queue = [];\nfunction emit(evt) {\n  if (socket && socket.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) socket.send(JSON.stringify(evt));\n  else queue.push(evt);\n}\nfunction flush() {\n  while (queue.length && socket.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) socket.send(JSON.stringify(queue.shift()));\n}\nsocket.addEventListener(\"open\", flush);\n```\n\nShip #2 first. It stops the data loss even if the disconnects continue."
     ]
    },
    "status": "finished_successfully",
