  "e5278c50-eaa3-41c2-85f1-7dc5b5dffce6": {
   "id": "e5278c50-eaa3-41c2-85f1-7dc5b5dffce6",
   "message": {
    "id": "e5278c50-eaa3-41c2-85f1-7dc5b5dffce6",
    "author": {
     "role": "assistant",
     "name": null,
     "metadata": {}
    },
    "create_time": 1762982135.016,
    "update_time": null,
    "content": {
     "content_type": "text",
     "parts": [
      "Use the gaps you can see indirectly:\n\n1. **Per client, before 4:10:** you don't have seq numbers, but you have timestamps. Find disconnect intervals from your server's connect/disconnect logs per socket id (or per student id if you map sids to users).\n2. **Estimate the event rate** per student from the connected periods (events/sec in section B while connected, or use section A's rate during the same task as a reference).\n3. **Lost ≈ Σ (gap duration × rate)** per student.\n\n```python\nlost = (gaps.groupby(\"student\").gap_s.sum() * rate_per_s).sum()\nshare = lost / (observed + lost)\n```\n\nThat gives you a defensible \"~X% of section B telemetry before 16:10 was lost\" number for the paper/notes. Also flag affected windows so labelers know those 30 s windows may be incomplete."
     ]
    },
